# After the fight in the den. emil_wins: Zuleika, when Kiril died and Emil stood with the party. no_emil: Mirela,
# when Kiril is dead and Emil is too (the party turned on both, or broke Kiril's truce for the children).
# zuleika_after: Zuleika on later visits to Emil's den. THE CLIMAX: the region's one milestone is given here (or
# in kiril.dialogue's kiril_resolve, whichever ends the pack question first).

~ emil_wins
set pack_resolved
set pack_aftermath_done
set wolf_pack_leader = "emil"
quest wolves_in_the_hills emil_leads
Narrator: Kiril lies on the floor of his own den, and as he cools he forgets how to be a wolf: the fur goes, the snout goes, and what is left is a big, ordinary dead man.
Narrator: Zuleika comes out of the dark at a run, and stops just short of Emil, and then doesn't.
Zuleika: You stupid, stubborn old dog.
Emil: I know. I told you not to.
Emil: It's done. By the old law the pack is mine again. Kiril's favourites are dead or running down the Krezk road with their tails tucked. The rest are listening.
Emil: Hear me, then. We hunt deer. We keep to the high hills. We don't come when the castle whistles. And the children go home.
if not flag.den_children_freed
set den_children_freed
quest the_stolen_children freed
endif
Zuleika: I'll take them down the stream path to the Krezk road at first light. And the eldest has a bite on her arm she thinks nobody saw. I saw.
Zuleika: Wolfsbane and the right words, three nights running. By the moon it'll be a scar and a story. Nothing worse.
set mirela_cured
if not flag.wolf_den_milestone_reached
set wolf_den_milestone_reached
xp milestone
endif
if guest:ezmerelda
Ezmerelda: A pack that leaves children alone. I'll believe it when I've watched it for a year.
Emil: Watch, then, huntress. From a respectful distance.
endif
if tarokka.ally.npc == emil_toranescu
-> emil_ally
endif
-> emil_stays

~ emil_ally
Emil: The Vistani grandmother's cards. She told me once I'd die in chains, and she was nearly right. Now they say I'm to walk with you to the old man's door.
Zuleika: Then go. I held this den with you in silver. I can hold it with you out for a walk.
Emil: She means she never needed me.
Zuleika: I mean bring yourself back in one piece. Or most of the pieces.
quest find_the_ally found
interject name:kip_smudgewick: A werewolf. On our side. Lovely. I'll draw up a little agreement. Terms of non-biting. Nothing formal.
interject class:cleric: Mind the bite, and we'll get along.
Emil: I always mind the bite. That was the whole argument.
-> END

~ emil_stays
Emil: You've given me back my pack. I can't follow you to the castle; they'd be at each other's throats in a week without me, and at Zuleika's in two.
Emil: But if it ever comes to the end with the old man on the hill, and you need teeth at his gates, send word up this hill.
leave emil_toranescu
Zuleika: Here. My own brewing: the same thing that keeps the pack sleepy when I want them sleepy. Don't ask what's in it. Drink it when you're bleeding.
give potion_of_healing 2
-> END

~ no_emil
set pack_resolved
set pack_aftermath_done
set wolf_pack_leader = "none"
quest wolves_in_the_hills pack_broken
if tarokka.ally.npc == emil_toranescu
quest find_the_ally lost
endif
if not flag.den_children_freed
set den_children_freed
quest the_stolen_children freed
endif
if flag.den_broken
set emil_dead
Narrator: When it is over, the den is very quiet. Kiril, Emil, Zuleika and the last of the pack lie where they fell, and in death every one of them is only a man or a woman, and older than you thought.
else
Narrator: Kiril is dead. The wolves that are left go out of the cave mouth in a grey stream and don't stop running. Somewhere down the hill one of them howls, and none of the others answer.
endif
Narrator: The pole gate at the back of the den creaks open. A girl of about ten comes out first, holding a much smaller girl's hand, and three more children behind her in a line.
Mirela: Is it over? Are they all...?
* It's over. You're going home. -> home
* [Medicine DC 13] You're holding your arm strangely. Let me see it. -> bite_ok | bite_fail

~ home
Mirela: Krezk is down the stream path, then west on the road. We can find it. We're not little. Except Ana. Ana's little.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: You're not walking it alone, Mirela. Ana can ride on my shoulders. Everybody else, single file behind me.
Narrator: You walk them down to the road and as far as the first milestone, where Mirela takes over, counting heads every twenty paces like a sergeant on a march.
if not flag.wolf_den_milestone_reached
set wolf_den_milestone_reached
xp milestone
endif
approve godrick_pendlebrook +2 kip_smudgewick +2 thistle +2: You walked the stolen children down to the road home
-> END

~ bite_ok
set mirela_bite_seen
Narrator: Under the torn sleeve, a bite: half healed, ringed in angry red, the marks of long teeth. She glares at you as if you'd made it yourself.
Mirela: Don't tell the little ones. Is it going to make me one of them?
* [Cleric] (Take her arm and pray over it.) -> bite_prayer
* We'll find you a priest in Krezk. -> bite_later

~ bite_fail
Narrator: She snatches her arm away and tucks it into her coat, and looks at you the way she looked at the wolves.
-> home

~ bite_prayer
set mirela_cured
Narrator: The prayer is short and plain, and for once in this valley something seems to be listening. The red ring around the bite fades, slowly, like a blush.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: The dawn comes, little one. Even here. Even to a bitten arm.
Mirela: It doesn't itch any more. It always itched.
inspire class:cleric: prayed the wolf's bite out of a child's arm
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 kip_smudgewick +1 thistle +1: You cured Mirela's bite before it took her
-> home

~ bite_later
Mirela: The priest in Krezk is old and his hands shake. But he's kind. I'll make him do it right.
-> home

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Later visits to Emil's den

~ zuleika_after
if guest:emil_toranescu
Zuleika: You've still got him, then. Feed him properly. He sulks when he's hungry, and he bites when he sulks.
else
Zuleika: The pack's mending fences. Literally; I have them mending the pen into a woodshed. Wolves hate mending things. It's very good for them.
endif
if flag.den_children_freed
Zuleika: The children got home. All five. The eldest scolded the Krezk gate guard for keeping them waiting.
endif
-> END
